        "original_id": "bc1c5874-a9bd-58ff-b6a7-4e3163db6d4e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lithocarpus, Duranta\n- Taxonomy: Fagaceae, Quercus\n- Concepts: plant morphology, native range, species count\n\nFacts:\n- Lithocarpus is a genus in the beech family Fagaceae.\n- Lithocarpus differs from Quercus by having erect spikes of insect-pollinated male flowers.\n- Lithocarpus differs from Quercus by having female flowers with short styles and punctate stigmas.\n- Duranta contains 17 species of shrubs and small trees.\n- Duranta is native from southern Florida to Mexico and South America.",
